<!--
  ANDROID 12+ (API 31+) BACKUP AND DEVICE-TRANSFER POLICY.

  WHAT IS IN THIS APP'S PRIVATE STORAGE. Every glucose reading the user has
  ever taken, every insulin dose and every meal they logged, the calibration
  history of their sensors / and, in the settings store, the sync credential
  that authenticates this phone to the account on the server. That last one
  is not merely private data: it is the key to all the rest of it, sitting on
  the server, for as long as the account exists.

  WHY android:allowBackup="false" IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN. allowBackup
  governs backup. From Android 12 the transfer paths were SPLIT: cloud backup
  (Google Drive / auto backup) and DEVICE-TO-DEVICE transfer / the copy made
  when the user sets up a new phone from an old one / are separate channels
  with separate rules, and the platform decides what an app that supplies no
  <data-extraction-rules> gets on each channel. That default has not been the
  same on every release, and it is not ours to choose by omission. An app
  whose files are a medical record should not be depending on which way a
  vendor's setup wizard happened to jump.

  WHAT THIS FILE SAYS. Nothing leaves this device by either channel. Both
  <cloud-backup> and <device-transfer> exclude every domain the platform can
  reach: the app's root directory, its files/, its databases, its shared
  preferences, its external-storage area, and the device-protected-storage
  (device_*) twins of each / which are separate domains precisely because
  they survive a locked boot, and which an "exclude root" alone does not
  cover. Enumerated rather than summarised, because a domain nobody wrote
  down is a domain that is included.

  IF DATA MUST EVER BE MOVED BETWEEN PHONES, it goes through EXPORT DATA and
  the sync server, where the user chooses it, sees it happen, and where the
  credential is re-established on the new device rather than copied to it.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
  <cloud-backup>
    <exclude domain="root" />
    <exclude domain="file" />
    <exclude domain="database" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
    <exclude domain="external" />
    <exclude domain="device_root" />
    <exclude domain="device_file" />
    <exclude domain="device_database" />
    <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" />
  </cloud-backup>
  <device-transfer>
    <exclude domain="root" />
    <exclude domain="file" />
    <exclude domain="database" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
    <exclude domain="external" />
    <exclude domain="device_root" />
    <exclude domain="device_file" />
    <exclude domain="device_database" />
    <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" />
  </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
